CSS helps with the styling of your webpage
selectors helps with mostly the targetting that is what element are we styling
Declaration refers to what is inside the braces
 Inline css is css written inside an html file
 internal ccs is css written inside a style document in an html document
 External css is css placed in an external file 
 Class is when you are targeting selected  elements
 Attribute selectors target elements based on their attribute
 Grouping selctors are selectors that target several elements
 Comments help us to shed more light on the css file
 Css cascade refers to the system that css uses to style a system when many rules are involved
 so the rules are importance, specifity and inheritance



    